## Files

`daily/year=YYYY/data.parquet` and `hourly/year=YYYY/data.parquet` hold the
rows up to the month before the recent months; the recent months (the month
of the day after the latest day and the month before) are in
`daily/year=YYYY/YYYY-MM.parquet` and `hourly/year=YYYY/YYYY-MM.parquet`.
The current month is updated every day; when a month ends, the monthly
update (the 1st, 20:00 JST) merges the oldest month file into its year file. Read `daily/*/*.parquet` to get all
rows. `manifest.json` lists the latest date and the month files with their
missing days.

## Notes

- Station ids are obsdl ids: `s` + WMO-style 5 digits for official stations, `a` + 4 digits for AMeDAS stations.
- Station positions are the current (or last) positions given in degrees and 0.1 minutes; past relocations are not reflected.
- AMeDAS sunshine duration since March 2021 is estimated from satellite data by JMA.
- JMA corrects past values from time to time. The last days are fetched again every day and the month before once more after it ended (then it moves into its year file); older years are not fetched again (applying JMA's announced corrections is planned).
